{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts","id":1192005,"title":"Are there any anime/manga/light novel characters that could be beasts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-05T11:40:36-08:00","id":1192005,"title":"Are there any anime/manga/light novel characters that could be beasts?","content":"I think guts from beserk? A predator Anakim with his SOUL being the beast of darkness/hellhound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T11:53:19-08:00","id":1192008,"title":"","content":"Check out The Devil is a Part-Timer. That one is pretty good Beast inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T12:06:08-08:00","id":1192017,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head:<ul><li>Yuu from <i>Owari no Seraph</i></li> <li>Akria from <i>Devilman Crybaby</i></li> <li>Naruto and the rest of the jinchuuriki from <i>Naruto </i> and <i>Naruto Shippuuden</i></li> <li>Rin and Yukio Okumura from <i>Blue Exorcist</i></li> <li>Inuyasha from <i>Inuyasha</i></li> <li>Any of the Metal Vessel users from the <i>Magi</i> series</li> <li>Lelouch vi Britannia from <i>Code Geass</i>, if you interpret his Geass as a Nightmare</li> <li>Sebastian from <i>Black Butler</i></li> <li>The Ajin from <i>Ajin: Demi-Human</i></li> <li>Kaneki and the rest of the ghouls from <i>Tokyo Ghoul</i>, particularly Jason.</li> </ul>EDIT:<ul><li>Just the Persona anime (and games) in general.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-05-2018, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T12:11:30-08:00","id":1192020,"title":"","content":"What type of beast would Kaneki from Tokyo ghoul be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T12:15:59-08:00","id":1192021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1192008#post1192008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out The Devil is a Part-Timer. That one is pretty good Beast inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div> you read the light novels? It does seem to be a comedic beast story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T12:37:49-08:00","id":1192030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1192020#post1192020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What type of beast would Kaneki from Tokyo ghoul be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say an Eshmaki or possibly Namtaru Predator, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T12:41:53-08:00","id":1192032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1192030#post1192030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say an Eshmaki or possibly Namtaru Predator, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that and what type of beast would other Tokyo ghoul characters be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T13:37:51-08:00","id":1192044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1192021#post1192021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> you read the light novels? It does seem to be a comedic beast story</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve read the first 7. I haven\u2019t gotten ahold of 8 yet. I absolutely love them, though. I started with the anime, and my wife and I both thought it seemed like a good Beast story. I enjoyed the cartoon enough that I sought out the light novels, and I have no regrets. I haven\u2019t read the mangas yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T14:36:45-08:00","id":1192064,"title":"","content":"Seconding Persona series. Especially 5. Palaces and the \u2018demonic\u2019 Shadows you fight as boss battles are good inspiration for Lairs and Horrors.<br /> <br /> (Persona 3 works for Geist inspiration. Persona 4, 1, and 2 aren\u2019t so clear a fit, but you can get there.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-05-2018, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T18:40:17-08:00","id":1192103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1192032#post1192032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is that and what type of beast would other Tokyo ghoul characters be?</div> </div> </div> </div>We had whole topic on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/561573-tokyo-ghoul-as-beast-game\">Tokyo Ghoul series as BtP inspiration</a> - with characters Families, Hungers or Atavisms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T21:09:40-08:00","id":1193804,"title":"","content":"Also on the Inspiration thread but Neuro from Majin Tantei Nogami Neuro is defiantly more of a Beast than a Demon, am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T01:49:45-08:00","id":1193847,"title":"","content":"While a bit of a stretch in points, Overlord could serve with some ideas. Specifically, Sebas Tian, who has a Hunger for Punishment if the latest episode is anything to go by. While he is indeed going out of his way to teach (harsh) lessons, accepting that they might kill the learner, those seem to be disconnected from his Hunger, so not applicable.<br /> His Atavisms would be Cyclopean Strength, Limb from Limb and Eye of Heaven, maybe Lightning Strike from what we've seen so far. I'd say he's probably a benevolent Anakim. His Horror is most likely his true form (he's some sort of Draconid, apparently). If his battle-aura is anything to go by, his Lair-traits would be ice-based. Pure WMG but could be Overgrowth and Extreme Cold.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Naberal Gamma could be an Inguma Predator, her Horror a shapeshifting Doppelganger. Her Atavisms are Enemy Within, Alien Mindset, Lightning Strike and Storm-Lashed, possibly also Wings of the Raptor (to represent Fly).<br /> <br /> Ainz is a Mage for sure, don't see a way to represent him as a Beast. Still, he'd be the Apex of Ainz Ool Gown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 03-10-2018, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T02:09:37-08:00","id":1193853,"title":"","content":"It's less the 'Beast' aspect and more the feel of the thing, but I can't help but feel that HOMRA from <i>K Project </i>would make for a good example for a more casual Primordial Cult. Mikoto Suoh is the Beast, and the rest are pyrokinetic psychics of various brands that he's gathered to himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T02:57:50-08:00","id":1193860,"title":"","content":"Or alternatively Guts from Berserk is a Hero hunting a Ugallu Tyrant Apex in the form of Griffith.<br /> <br /> It also goes without saying that all the Apostles are Beasts, most of them being Namtaru and Eshmaki Predators. However the elite Apostles of the Neo Band of the Hawk are all Apexs (is that the plural for Apex?) gathered from around the world under Griffith's banner.<br /> <br /> Zod and Grunbeld are Anakim Nemeses, considering they both see Guts as a worthy adversary and have a code of honor in battle.<br /> <br /> Mr &quot;One day I'll take your pretty head&quot; Rakshas is definitely a Makara Whispers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T05:36:45-08:00","id":1193888,"title":"","content":"Ajin seems to be good inspiration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T18:39:28-08:00","id":1194113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1193860#post1193860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or alternatively Guts from Berserk is a Hero hunting a Ugallu Tyrant Apex in the form of Griffith.<br /> <br /> It also goes without saying that all the Apostles are Beasts, most of them being Namtaru and Eshmaki Predators. However the elite Apostles of the Neo Band of the Hawk are all Apexs (is that the plural for Apex?) gathered from around the world under Griffith's banner.<br /> <br /> Zod and Grunbeld are Anakim Nemeses, considering they both see Guts as a worthy adversary and have a code of honor in battle.<br /> <br /> Mr &quot;One day I'll take your pretty head&quot; Rakshas is definitely a Makara Whispers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely agreeing here, except Griffith seems like a poster child for an Incarnate, especially following the aptly-named Incarnation Ceremony. Emperor Ganishka tried going down the same path, except he botched it and became a Rampant instead. You may see the rest of the God Hand as either Unfettered that kept their minds, or Incarnates that prefer to roam the Primordial Dream all the time rather than coming back to the mundane world. In either case, they have Legendary Horror. Their M.O. seems most fitting for Enticers. Void seems more like an Anakim, Slan looks like a Makara, Conrad seems Namtaru, and Ubik is Eshmaki. The Skull Knight is a Hero that achieved the equivalent of Inversion for Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-11-2018, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T19:58:34-08:00","id":1194121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1194113#post1194113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Largely agreeing here, except Griffith seems like a poster child for an Incarnate, especially following the aptly-named Incarnation Ceremony. Emperor Ganishka tried going down the same path, except he botched it and became a Rampant instead. You may see the rest of the God Hand as either Unfettered that kept their minds, or Incarnates that prefer to roam the Primordial Dream all the time rather than coming back to the mundane world. I either case, they have Legendary Horrors. Their M.O. seems most fitting for Enticers. Void seems more like an Anakim, Slan looks like a Makara, Conrad seems Namtaru, and Ubik is Eshmaki. The Skull Knight is a Hero that achieved the equivalent of Inversion for Heroes,</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWouldn't inversion for a Hero be transforming into a Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T22:26:21-08:00","id":1194139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangaholic13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1194121#post1194121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWouldn't inversion for a Hero be transforming into a Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose so. If you think about it, it seems fitting for what the Skull Knight became, and the path Gatsu might be going down to, if he listens to the Hellhound. Anyway, the SK seems rather close to if not exactly the equal of the God Hand in terms of power. So I'd guess the power tier of the Berserk setting might go this way, in Begotten terms:<br /> Tier 4<br /> Idea of Evil avatar of the Dark Mother, or whatever Astral equivalent of the Ascended/Exarchs the Begotten may get.<br /> Tier 3.<br /> the God Hand, Griffith, Skull Knight, Emperor Ganishka various kinds of Inheritance Beasts. Griffith is the Incarnate Ugallu Tyrant poster child, the GD is a Brood of Enticer Incarnates or Unfettered of various Families that kept their mind, the Skull Knight is a Anakim Nemesis Incarnate or Rampant that kept his mind, Ganishka is a vanilla Merger Tyrant (family may vary between Anakim, Namtaru, and Ugallu).<br /> Tier 2<br /> Guts. He's either a high-powered Hero (with the Berserker Armor as an Artifact that is slowly turning him into a Beast) or a high-Lair Nemesis Beast (I'd guess Anakim or Makara).<br /> Tier 1<br /> The Apostles. Vanilla Beasts, the whole of them. All Families seem represented in their ranks, although Anakim, Namtaru, and Makara seem the most prevalent. Most of them look like Predators, Tyrants, or Ravagers.<br /> <br /> Plus the witches, that are obviously Mages. Schierke made a Family Tie with Guts, and Flora had one with the Skull Knight. The rest of the human characters seem mortals, they are too helpless and useless to be anything else. Ivalera is probably a Goetia or Spirit that got bound to Schierke as a Familiar. I'm not sure what to make of Puck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-11-2018, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T05:53:43-07:00","id":1194224,"title":"","content":"And the ritual of merged worlds brought about when the Skull Knight accidentally struck Ganishka instead of Femto is the Primordial Dream manifesting itself in the material world. The Sea God that Guts faced on the way to Elfhelm was an Unfettered Makara bought back into the material world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 03-11-2018, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T09:23:20-07:00","id":1194269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1194224#post1194224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the ritual of merged worlds brought about when the Skull Knight accidentally struck Ganishka instead of Femto is the Primordial Dream manifesting itself in the material world. The Sea God that Gut's faced on the way to Elfhelm was an Unfettered Makara bought back into the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd say Fantasia is a fusion of the material world with a large portion of the 'public' layers of the Astral (Temenos, Primordial Dream, and Anima Mundi) as a whole, rather than just the PD, due to the manifestation of Falkovnia and various magical beings and phenomena that do not seem especially nightmarish, but yeah. And Griffith, as an high-powered Incarnate that probably has Legendary Horror, seems able to open temporary portals to yet other realms (such as the Underworld and the Shadow) and command the inhabitants thereof, such as when he causes the ghosts of Falkovnia's inhabitants' dead relatives to appear.<br /> <br /> The deep layer of the Astral where the Idea of Evil resides was not included in the fusion. It seems an intersection of the Astral with the Underworld, since both godlike Goetia entities and hordes of restless dead exist there. Unless it is an intersection with the Abyss instead, and the IoE is an Annunaki pushing its way into the Tellurian and corrupting it with its notion of evil for evil's sake to explain suffering in the world. It might help explain the exceptionally crappy state of the Berserk world, even for CoD standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-11-2018, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T15:15:41-07:00","id":1196239,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, I didn't see anyone mentioning the Witch girls from PMMM. They succumbed to their worst nightmares ere saved by a female goddess figure, and can appear as normal humans or summon a terrifically powerful ephemeral avatar of their worst nightmares that also imposes a weird overlayed partition on reality around them, sometimes with things comparable to thralls and minions. Seems totally spot on to me.<br /> <br /> (Caveat: &quot;nightmare&quot; should be taken as synonymous with &quot;highly phantasmagoric and symbolic manifestation of rage, despair, spite, or whatever dragged up from, presumably, their subconscious&quot; as even &quot;dreams&quot; and &quot;nightmares&quot; in the Beast parlance don't have a totally consistent definition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T19:25:06-07:00","id":1196318,"title":"","content":"Light Yagami from Death Note ? Ryuk is his Horror, he hungers for Punishment, L is a Hero, and those who follow Kira a Primordial Cult ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T19:34:21-07:00","id":1196324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192005-are-there-any-anime-manga-light-novel-characters-that-could-be-beasts?p=1196318#post1196318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Light Yagami from Death Note ? Ryuk is his Horror, he hungers for Punishment, L is a Hero, and those who follow Kira a Primordial Cult ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b... Given the things he planned t